{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --stat; git diff -- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md; nl -ba test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc | sed -n '1090,1390p'\"","aggregated_output":" docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md |  35 +++-\n src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                  |  35 ++--\n src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc            |  63 ++++++-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc            |  29 +++-\n test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc           | 293 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 5 files changed, 426 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md b/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md\nindex a88f2a19..789579ad 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md\n+++ b/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md\n@@ -166,12 +166,29 @@ published snapshot: both are HEAD naming an older valid manifest, which\n opens and recovers.\n \n What the open recovered — `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the\n-walked snapshot or nil>}` — is exposed as `:recovery` on the store\n-handle and `:index-recovery` on the shell state, for the rehydration\n-slice. Nothing installs it yet: `q` in a new session answers from that\n-session's own publications, and `(reset)` keeps today's rebuild\n-semantics. Restoring the transaction log, initializing the indexer from\n-the snapshot, and `(reset)` continuity in durable mode are that slice,\n-not this one. Until it lands, a restarted (or reset) session's first\n-publication covers only its own facts, so HEAD moves off the previous\n-snapshot; the older blobs stay in `content.jing`, unreferenced.\n+walked snapshot or nil>}` — is `:recovery` on the store handle and\n+`:index-recovery` on the shell state, and the shell installs it before\n+it admits any evaluation (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`). The indexer's\n+log becomes a fresh complete-retention memory log holding the recovered\n+datoms as transaction records, one per original `t` in ascending order,\n+each datom and its `t` preserved, so the round's transactor keeps\n+deriving the next `t` from it. Entity allocation resumes one past the\n+greatest restored entity or metadata id (never below\n+`datom/first-user-id`), so restored and new ids never collide. The\n+recovered manifest is the indexer's published one and its transaction\n+counts are the restored ones, so `q` answers the previous run's facts\n+before any new evaluation, and the first publication after a restart\n+covers old and new facts — HEAD moves to a manifest holding both.\n+\n+Every process start mints a new shell token. Restored facts keep their\n+original session tokens and root and round metadata, since they are the\n+datoms as committed; new facts carry the new token, so `q` over the\n+history view tells the runs apart.\n+\n+With a durable store, `(reset)` and VM selection rebuild the VM, the\n+expander, and their observers, but the new indexer continues the old\n+one's log, entity allocation, counts, and published manifest\n+(`yin.repl.index/carry-over`): they never reset `t` or entity\n+allocation, and the published index stays queryable once\n+`dao.space.query` is required again. With the default memory store they\n+start an empty index, exactly as before.\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\nindex bd187129..009a42f9 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n@@ -816,9 +816,12 @@\n \n    `:index-recovery` carries what the durable open recovered —\n    `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the validated snapshot or nil>}`\n-   — exposed for the rehydration slice; nothing installs it yet, so `q`\n-   answers from this session's own publications and `(reset)` keeps\n-   today's rebuild semantics.\"\n+   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\n+   is admitted (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): `q` answers the previous\n+   run's facts, which keep their own session tokens, while this process\n+   mints a new token for its own.  In durable mode `(reset)` and `(vm …)`\n+   carry the index across the rebuild; with the memory store they start\n+   an empty one, as they always have.\"\n   ([] (create-state {}))\n   ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n             content-store content-client name-env link-policy index-store\n@@ -846,7 +849,9 @@\n                         :content-store content-store\n                         :content-client content-client})]\n      (merge\n-       (make-session vm-type output-stream primitives shell-token index-store)\n+       (update (make-session vm-type output-stream primitives shell-token\n+                             index-store)\n+               :indexer index/rehydrate (:recovery index-store))\n        {:lang lang\n         :vm-type vm-type\n         :extra-primitives primitives\n@@ -1520,13 +1525,20 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n    names a code segment the old VM held, which the new one does not.  The\n    new expander holds only the standard forms.  A require still pending\n    on the old VM is dropped with it: its link pair is the session's, and\n-   the new session answers from its own.\"\n+   the new session answers from its own.\n+\n+   Over a durable store the code index is not the session's to drop: the\n+   new indexer continues the old one's log, entity allocation, and\n+   published manifest (`yin.repl.index/carry-over`), so a rebuild never\n+   resets `t`.  Over the memory store it starts empty, as it always has.\"\n   [state vm-type]\n   (merge state\n-         (make-session vm-type (:output-stream state)\n-                       (:extra-primitives state)\n-                       (:shell-token state)\n-                       (:index-store state))\n+         (cond-> (make-session vm-type (:output-stream state)\n+                               (:extra-primitives state)\n+                               (:shell-token state)\n+                               (:index-store state))\n+           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n+           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n          {:vm-type vm-type\n           :ingress-loss? false\n           :last-value nil\n@@ -1547,7 +1559,10 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n       vm (let [vm-type (first args)]\n            (if (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n              [(rebuild-session state vm-type)\n-              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type) \" (store cleared)\")]\n+              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type)\n+                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n+                     \" (VM store cleared; durable code index kept)\"\n+                     \" (store cleared)\"))]\n              [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL VM type \" (pr-str vm-type)\n                          \"; supported: \"\n                          (pr-str (vec (keys vm-constructors))))]))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc\nindex 5be82eae..15cf7cf0 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc\n@@ -41,7 +41,10 @@\n    round lost for the shell's round result, and `status` is the\n    evaluator-independent view `repl-state` reports.  Everything here is a\n    session-composition value; reset and VM selection rebuild it with the\n-   session.\"\n+   session.  Over a durable store a new process's indexer is seeded from\n+   the recovered snapshot (`rehydrate`), and a rebuilt session's continues\n+   the old one's index (`carry-over`), so `t` and entity allocation never\n+   restart there.\"\n   (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n             [dao.jing :as jing]\n             [dao.space.index :as index]\n@@ -167,6 +170,64 @@\n    :failure nil})\n \n \n+(defn- next-entity-id\n+  \"One greater than the greatest entity or metadata-entity id `datoms`\n+   use, never below `datom/first-user-id`.\"\n+  [datoms]\n+  (reduce (fn [next-e [e _a _v _t m]]\n+            (cond-> next-e\n+              (integer? e) (max (inc e))\n+              (integer? m) (max (inc m))))\n+          datom/first-user-id\n+          datoms))\n+\n+\n+(defn rehydrate\n+  \"Seed a fresh indexer from a recovered durable snapshot, `{:manifest\n+   address :datoms [...]}` (yin.repl.store's `:recovery`), before any\n+   evaluation is admitted.  Its log becomes a fresh complete-retention\n+   memory log holding the recovered datoms as transaction records, one\n+   per original `t` in ascending order, each datom and its `t` preserved,\n+   so the round's transactor keeps deriving the next `t` from it.  Entity\n+   allocation resumes one past the greatest restored entity or metadata\n+   id.  The manifest is the published one, covering every restored\n+   transaction, so `q` answers from it before anything new is evaluated.\n+   Restored facts keep their original session tokens and round metadata:\n+   they are the datoms as committed.  A recovery without a manifest is an\n+   empty index and leaves the indexer as it is.\"\n+  [indexer {:keys [manifest datoms]}]\n+  (if (nil? manifest)\n+    indexer\n+    (let [log (memory-log)\n+          by-t (group-by index/datom-t datoms)\n+          ts (sort (keys by-t))]\n+      (doseq [t ts]\n+        (let [answer (stream/append! log {:dao.space/transaction\n+                                          {:t t, :datoms (vec (get by-t t))}})]\n+          (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n+            (throw (ex-info \"the recovered snapshot could not be rehydrated\"\n+                            {:t t, :outcome answer})))))\n+      (assoc indexer\n+             :local log\n+             :next-e (next-entity-id datoms)\n+             :transactions (count ts)\n+             :published (count ts)\n+             :manifest-address manifest))))\n+\n+\n+(defn carry-over\n+  \"A rebuilt session's fresh `indexer`, continuing `previous`'s index: its\n+   transaction log, entity allocation, counts, and published manifest.\n+   `(reset)` and VM selection over a durable store use it, so a rebuild\n+   never resets `t` or entity allocation and `q` keeps answering the\n+   published index; the observer is the new session's, and a lost or\n+   failed indexer is recovered by the rebuild as it is today.\"\n+  [indexer previous]\n+  (merge indexer\n+         (select-keys previous [:local :next-e :transactions :published\n+                                :published-payloads :manifest-address])))\n+\n+\n (defn- open-publication\n   \"The round's transactor and the `dao.jing` pool observer over its intake.\n    `transactor/create!` derives the next `t` from `:local`'s retained\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc\nindex 788baf18..a17f2816 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n (ns yin.repl.store\n   \"Startup selection and durable lifecycle of the code index's store\n    (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md; the durable-store startup\n-   contract, slices 1-2).\n+   contract, slices 1-3).\n \n    The store is chosen once, before the shell composes: `mem` — a fresh\n    in-memory `dao.jing` store, today's behaviour — or `file:<dir>`, the\n@@ -21,13 +21,16 @@\n    absent HEAD is an empty index while a malformed HEAD, a missing\n    manifest, or an unreadable index node refuses startup rather than\n    starting empty.  A round that publishes moves HEAD only after its\n-   manifest is read back (`:head-fn`), and the recovery it leaves is\n-   exposed as `:recovery` for the rehydration slice.\n-\n-   Rehydration itself is not this slice.  The recovered facts are exposed,\n-   not installed: `q` in a new session answers from that session's own\n-   publications until slice 3 rebuilds the indexer from `:recovery`, and\n-   `(reset)` keeps today's rebuild semantics.\"\n+   manifest is read back (`:head-fn`), and what the open recovered is\n+   `:recovery`.\n+\n+   The shell installs that recovery before it admits any evaluation\n+   (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): the indexer's log, entity allocation,\n+   counts, and published manifest continue the previous run's, so `q`\n+   answers the old facts, new transactions continue `t`, and the next\n+   HEAD covers old and new facts.  A durable store (`durable?`) also\n+   carries the index across `(reset)` and VM selection; the memory store\n+   keeps today's empty rebuild.\"\n   (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n                        [clojure.edn :as edn]])\n             #?(:cljd nil\n@@ -367,7 +370,7 @@\n    content log; `:head-fn`, `(fn [manifest-address])`, the atomic HEAD\n    write a round performs after its manifest is read back; `:recovery`,\n    `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the walked snapshot or nil>}`,\n-   exposed for the rehydration slice; and `:durable-dir`, the directory\n+   which the shell rehydrates its indexer from; and `:durable-dir`, the directory\n    an operator's refusal can name.\"\n   [spec]\n   (let [checked (checked-spec spec)]\n@@ -388,6 +391,14 @@\n                    :durable-dir dir)))))))\n \n \n+(defn durable?\n+  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store `open` answered: its\n+   published index outlives the process, so a session rebuild continues\n+   it rather than starting an empty one.\"\n+  [store]\n+  (some? (:durable-dir store)))\n+\n+\n (defn close!\n   \"Release the store's lifecycle resources — the content log handle and,\n    in durable mode, the directory lock.  Nothing further can be read or\n  1090\t            [two _] (repl/eval-input one \"(+ 2 3)\")]\n  1091\t        (is (not= first-manifest (get-in two [:indexer :manifest-address])))\n  1092\t        (store/close! (:index-store two))\n  1093\t        ;; The crash rewound HEAD to the first round: the second round's\n  1094\t        ;; blobs are unreferenced now.\n  1095\t        (write-text! (head-path dir)\n  1096\t                     (str \"{:version 1, :manifest \" first-manifest \"}\"))\n  1097\t        (let [reopened (store/open {:type :file :dir dir})]\n  1098\t          (is (= first-manifest (get-in reopened [:recovery :manifest])))\n  1099\t          (is (= first-committed (set (:datoms (:recovery reopened)))))\n  1100\t          (store/close! reopened)))\n  1101\t      (finally\n  1102\t        (cleanup-dir! dir)))))\n  1103\t\n  1104\t\n  1105\t;; =============================================================================\n  1106\t;; Rehydration and (reset) continuity — slice 3.  The restart sequence of\n  1107\t;; the durable-store ruling (§5), as the REPL input lines an operator types:\n  1108\t;; evaluate, stop, restart on the same directory, require dao.space.query,\n  1109\t;; query the old facts, evaluate more, query both.\n  1110\t;; =============================================================================\n  1111\t\n  1112\t(def ^:private require-line\n  1113\t  \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n  1114\t\n  1115\t\n  1116\t(defn- q-line\n  1117\t  [query & more]\n  1118\t  (str \"(dao.space.query/q (quote \" (pr-str query) \")\"\n  1119\t       (apply str (map #(str \" \" %) more))\n  1120\t       \")\"))\n  1121\t\n  1122\t\n  1123\t(defn- evaluate\n  1124\t  [state lines]\n  1125\t  (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\n  1126\t            (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\n  1127\t              [state' (conj texts text)]))\n  1128\t          [state []]\n  1129\t          lines))\n  1130\t\n  1131\t\n  1132\t(defn- provenance-line\n  1133\t  \"A history-view query for the session token and t of the literal\n  1134\t   `value` — a constant only one def carries.  It sits inside the quoted\n  1135\t   query, never as an input, so the calling line's own literals (every\n  1136\t   program is indexed, the calling one included) cannot match it.\"\n  1137\t  [value]\n  1138\t  (q-line [:find '?s '?t\n  1139\t           :where ['?e :yin/value value '?t '?m]\n  1140\t           ['?m :yin.repl/session '?s '?t1 '?m1]]\n  1141\t          \"{:view :history}\"))\n  1142\t\n  1143\t\n  1144\t(defn- provenance\n  1145\t  \"The `[token t]` pairs a provenance answer's text names.\"\n  1146\t  [text]\n  1147\t  (set (map (fn [[_ token t]] [token (read-edn t)])\n  1148\t            (re-seq #\"\\[\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\" (\\d+)\\]\" (str text)))))\n  1149\t\n  1150\t\n  1151\t(defn- local-datoms\n  1152\t  \"Every datom of the indexer's retained transaction log.\"\n  1153\t  [state]\n  1154\t  (mapcat :datoms (transactions state)))\n  1155\t\n  1156\t\n  1157\t(defn- ids-of\n  1158\t  \"The entity and metadata-entity ids a datom set uses.\"\n  1159\t  [datoms]\n  1160\t  (into #{}\n  1161\t        (comp (mapcat (fn [[e _a _v _t m]] [e m]))\n  1162\t              (filter #(and (integer? %) (<= datom/first-user-id %))))\n  1163\t        datoms))\n  1164\t\n  1165\t\n  1166\t(deftest a-restarted-durable-shell-answers-q-with-the-previous-runs-facts\n  1167\t  (let [dir (temp-dir)\n  1168\t        spec {:type :file :dir dir}]\n  1169\t    (try\n  1170\t      (let [[first-run _] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:index-store-spec spec})\n  1171\t                                    [\"(def alpha 1001)\"])\n  1172\t            first-token (:shell-token first-run)\n  1173\t            first-datoms (set (local-datoms first-run))\n  1174\t            _ (store/close! (:index-store first-run))\n  1175\t            restarted (repl/create-state {:index-store-spec spec})\n  1176\t            [second-run [required old-only _ both-alpha both-beta]]\n  1177\t            (evaluate restarted\n  1178\t                      [require-line\n  1179\t                       (provenance-line 1001)\n  1180\t                       \"(def beta 2002)\"\n  1181\t                       (provenance-line 1001)\n  1182\t                       (provenance-line 2002)])\n  1183\t            second-token (:shell-token second-run)\n  1184\t            [[_ alpha-t]] (vec (provenance both-alpha))\n  1185\t            [[_ beta-t]] (vec (provenance both-beta))]\n  1186\t        (is (= \"'dao.space.query\" required))\n  1187\t        (testing \"the restarted shell is seeded before any evaluation\"\n  1188\t          (let [status (:index (repl/repl-state restarted))]\n  1189\t            (is (= (count (transactions first-run)) (:transactions status))\n  1190\t                \"the restored transactions are counted\")\n  1191\t            (is (true? (:published? status))\n  1192\t                \"and published: q can answer before any new program\")))\n  1193\t        (is (not= first-token second-token)\n  1194\t            \"every process start mints its own shell token\")\n  1195\t        (testing \"q sees the old facts before any new evaluation\"\n  1196\t          (is (= #{first-token} (set (map first (provenance old-only))))\n  1197\t              old-only))\n  1198\t        (testing \"q sees old and new facts, with increasing t and distinct\n  1199\t                  session provenance\"\n  1200\t          (is (= #{first-token} (set (map first (provenance both-alpha))))\n  1201\t              both-alpha)\n  1202\t          (is (= #{second-token} (set (map first (provenance both-beta))))\n  1203\t              both-beta)\n  1204\t          (is (and alpha-t beta-t (< alpha-t beta-t))\n  1205\t              \"the new transactions continue t from the restored log\"))\n  1206\t        (testing \"restored entity ids never collide with new ones\"\n  1207\t          (let [new-datoms (remove first-datoms (local-datoms second-run))]\n  1208\t            (is (seq new-datoms))\n  1209\t            (is (empty? (cset/intersection (ids-of first-datoms)\n  1210\t                                                  (ids-of new-datoms))))))\n  1211\t        (testing \"the first post-restart publication's HEAD covers old and\n  1212\t                  new facts\"\n  1213\t          (let [manifest (get-in second-run [:indexer :manifest-address])\n  1214\t                published (set (dao.index/read-datoms\n  1215\t                                 (:index-store second-run) manifest))]\n  1216\t            (is (= {:version 1 :manifest manifest} (head-record-of dir)))\n  1217\t            (is (every? published first-datoms) \"the old facts\")\n  1218\t            (is (every? published (local-datoms second-run))\n  1219\t                \"and every committed fact\")))\n  1220\t        (testing \"(reset) and (vm …) keep the facts, t and entity allocation\"\n  1221\t          (let [before (set (local-datoms second-run))\n  1222\t                [after-reset [_ _ alpha-after beta-after]]\n  1223\t                (evaluate second-run\n  1224\t                          [\"(reset)\" require-line\n  1225\t                           (provenance-line 1001) (provenance-line 2002)])\n  1226\t                [switched [_ _ gamma-text]]\n  1227\t                (evaluate after-reset\n  1228\t                          [\"(vm :stack)\" \"(def gamma 3003)\"\n  1229\t                           (provenance-line 3003)])\n  1230\t                [switched' [_ gamma-q]]\n  1231\t                (evaluate switched [require-line (provenance-line 3003)])\n  1232\t                [[_ gamma-t]] (vec (provenance gamma-q))\n  1233\t                gamma-datoms (remove before (local-datoms switched'))]\n  1234\t            (is (= (provenance both-alpha) (provenance alpha-after)))\n  1235\t            (is (= (provenance both-beta) (provenance beta-after)))\n  1236\t            (is (str/includes? (str gamma-text) \"Unable to resolve\")\n  1237\t                \"the switched session needs its own require\")\n  1238\t            (is (and gamma-t (< beta-t gamma-t)) gamma-q)\n  1239\t            (is (empty? (cset/intersection (ids-of before)\n  1240\t                                                  (ids-of gamma-datoms)))\n  1241\t                \"entity allocation continued across the rebuilds\")))\n  1242\t        (store/close! (:index-store second-run)))\n  1243\t      (finally\n  1244\t        (cleanup-dir! dir)))))\n  1245\t\n  1246\t\n  1247\t(deftest mem-mode-reset-still-starts-an-empty-index\n  1248\t  (let [[state [_ _ _ _ after-reset]]\n  1249\t        (evaluate (repl/create-state)\n  1250\t                  [\"(def alpha 1001)\" require-line (provenance-line 1001)\n  1251\t                   \"(reset)\"\n  1252\t                   require-line])\n  1253\t        [_ [alpha-after]] (evaluate state [(provenance-line 1001)])]\n  1254\t    (is (= \"'dao.space.query\" after-reset))\n  1255\t    (is (= \"#{}\" alpha-after)\n  1256\t        \"the memory store's reset keeps today's empty rebuild\")))\n  1257\t\n  1258\t\n  1259\t;; =============================================================================\n  1260\t;; Rehydration fidelity over a published fixture: several `t`, a retraction,\n  1261\t;; and a greatest id that occurs only in `m`.\n  1262\t;; =============================================================================\n  1263\t\n  1264\t(defn- memory-log!\n  1265\t  []\n  1266\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n  1267\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})))\n  1268\t\n  1269\t\n  1270\t(def ^:private fixture-txs\n  1271\t  \"Three transactions a real transactor commits as t 0, 1 and 2: two\n  1272\t   assertions; an assertion whose metadata entity, 40, is the greatest id\n  1273\t   and occurs nowhere but in `m`; and the retraction of the first fact.\"\n  1274\t  [[[16 :fixture/name \"a\" nil 1] [17 :fixture/name \"b\" nil 1]]\n  1275\t   [[18 :fixture/name \"c\" nil 40]]\n  1276\t   [[16 :fixture/name \"a\" nil 0]]])\n  1277\t\n  1278\t\n  1279\t(defn- publish-fixture!\n  1280\t  \"Commit `fixture-txs` through a transactor, publish the covered indexes\n  1281\t   into a fresh durable store at `dir`, drain them into it, move HEAD to\n  1282\t   the manifest as a round would, and close the store.  Answers the\n  1283\t   committed transaction records.\"\n  1284\t  [dir]\n  1285\t  (let [opened (store/open {:type :file :dir dir})\n  1286\t        local (memory-log!)\n  1287\t        intake (memory-log!)\n  1288\t        tx (transactor/create! {:local-stream local\n  1289\t                                :intake-pool [intake]\n  1290\t                                :name \"fixture\"})]\n  1291\t    (doseq [tx-data fixture-txs]\n  1292\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n  1293\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (transactor/transact! tx tx-data)))))\n  1294\t    (let [{:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! tx)]\n  1295\t      (loop [pool (jing/observer-state\n  1296\t                    [{:stream intake\n  1297\t                      :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n  1298\t                                (dao.stream/cursor intake :dao.stream/oldest))}])]\n  1299\t        (let [{:keys [signal state]} (jing/observe-step! opened pool)]\n  1300\t          (when (= :dao.stream/ok signal)\n  1301\t            (recur state))))\n  1302\t      ((:head-fn opened) manifest-address)\n  1303\t      (store/close! opened)\n  1304\t      (mapv :dao.space/transaction (stream-values local)))))\n  1305\t\n  1306\t\n  1307\t(defn- groups\n  1308\t  \"Transaction records as `t` -> the set of its datoms.\"\n  1309\t  [records]\n  1310\t  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [t datoms]}] [t (set datoms)])) records))\n  1311\t\n  1312\t\n  1313\t(def ^:private fixture-history\n  1314\t  '[:find ?e ?v ?t ?m :where [?e :fixture/name ?v ?t ?m]])\n  1315\t\n  1316\t\n  1317\t(def ^:private fixture-current\n  1318\t  '[:find ?e ?v :where [?e :fixture/name ?v]])\n  1319\t\n  1320\t\n  1321\t(deftest a-restart-restores-every-transaction-group-history-row-and-retraction\n  1322\t  (let [dir (temp-dir)]\n  1323\t    (try\n  1324\t      (let [committed (publish-fixture! dir)\n  1325\t            expected-groups (groups committed)\n  1326\t            history-rows (into #{}\n  1327\t                               (comp (mapcat :datoms)\n  1328\t                                     (map (fn [[e _a v t m]] [e v t m])))\n  1329\t                               committed)\n  1330\t            restarted (repl/create-state {:index-store-spec {:type :file\n  1331\t                                                             :dir dir}})\n  1332\t            ;; The log is a live stream the later rounds append to: read\n  1333\t            ;; the restored groups before anything is evaluated.\n  1334\t            restored-groups (groups (transactions restarted))\n  1335\t            [before [_ history current]]\n  1336\t            (evaluate restarted [require-line\n  1337\t                                 (q-line fixture-history \"{:view :history}\")\n  1338\t                                 (q-line fixture-current)])\n  1339\t            [after [_ history' current']]\n  1340\t            (evaluate before [\"(def delta 4004)\"\n  1341\t                              (q-line fixture-history \"{:view :history}\")\n  1342\t                              (q-line fixture-current)])]\n  1343\t        (is (= [0 1 2] (sort (keys expected-groups)))\n  1344\t            \"the fixture spans three transaction times\")\n  1345\t        (is (= expected-groups restored-groups)\n  1346\t            \"each restored transaction is its original group, at its t\")\n  1347\t        (testing \"before a new publication\"\n  1348\t          (is (= history-rows (read-edn history))\n  1349\t              \"history rows: every assertion and the retraction, each at its\n  1350\t               t and with its m\")\n  1351\t          (is (= #{[17 \"b\"] [18 \"c\"]} (read-edn current))\n  1352\t              \"the current view applies the retraction\"))\n  1353\t        (testing \"after a new publication\"\n  1354\t          (is (= expected-groups\n  1355\t                 (select-keys (groups (transactions after))\n  1356\t                              (keys expected-groups)))\n  1357\t              \"the restored groups are untouched\")\n  1358\t          (is (every? #(< 2 %) (remove (set (keys expected-groups))\n  1359\t                                       (keys (groups (transactions after)))))\n  1360\t              \"new transactions come after the restored ones\")\n  1361\t          (is (= history-rows (read-edn history')))\n  1362\t          (is (= #{[17 \"b\"] [18 \"c\"]} (read-edn current'))))\n  1363\t        (testing \"a greatest id only in m still bounds entity allocation\"\n  1364\t          (let [new-datoms (remove (set (mapcat :datoms committed))\n  1365\t                                   (local-datoms after))]\n  1366\t            (is (seq new-datoms))\n  1367\t            (is (every? #(< 40 %) (ids-of new-datoms))\n  1368\t                \"every id allocated after the restart exceeds m = 40\")))\n  1369\t        (store/close! (:index-store after)))\n  1370\t      (finally\n  1371\t        (cleanup-dir! dir)))))\n  1372\t\n  1373\t\n  1374\t(deftest vm-selection-says-what-it-keeps\n  1375\t  (let [dir (temp-dir)]\n  1376\t    (try\n  1377\t      (let [[durable [switched]] (evaluate (repl/create-state\n  1378\t                                             {:index-store-spec {:type :file\n  1379\t                                                                 :dir dir}})\n  1380\t                                           [\"(vm :stack)\"])\n  1381\t            [_ [switched-mem]] (evaluate (repl/create-state) [\"(vm :stack)\"])]\n  1382\t        (is (= (str \"Switched to DebruijnStackVM (VM store cleared; durable\"\n  1383\t                    \" code index kept)\")\n  1384\t               switched)\n  1385\t            \"in durable mode the code index survives the switch, and says so\")\n  1386\t        (is (= \"Switched to DebruijnStackVM (store cleared)\" switched-mem)\n  1387\t            \"the memory store's message is today's\")\n  1388\t        (store/close! (:index-store durable)))\n  1389\t      (finally\n  1390\t        (cleanup-dir! di